ARCHITECTURE

This folder documents tam-last's system architecture: the modules and how
they connect, the path a key press takes, the data structures, the
dependencies, and the evaluations of other terminals that shaped them.


FILES

  principles.md          the design rules every change follows
  key-path.md            every hop from a finger on a key to a program
                         reading bytes, and back to the screen: what
                         happens at each, and who controls it
  data-structures.md     the wire buffers, the screen, the font cache
                         and the keyboard state, as built today
  dependencies.md        every library tam-last uses, why, and which
                         version removes it
  foot-evaluation.md     how foot works; what to take and what not to
                         repeat

  Later phases add their own files here, for example scrollback.md
  (0.0.3) and kitty-keys.md (P2).


KEEPING IT TRUE

  These documents describe the code as it is. A change that alters a
  structure, an algorithm or a dependency updates the matching file in
  the same commit. Where code and document disagree, the code is right
  and the document is a bug.
